              "text": "The intensity of a sound wave passing through air is given by\nI = Kvρf²A² where I is the intensity (power per unit area),\nK is a constant without units, v is the speed of sound,\nρ is the density of air, f is the frequency of the wave and A is the amplitude of the wave.\nShow that both sides of the equation have the same SI base units.",
