                "hints": [
                  "The sphere's volume is expressed as πd³/6, so rearrange the supplied mass–density–volume expression to make d the subject before substituting numbers.",
                  "Substitute m = 7.5 kg and ρ = 8100 kg m⁻³ into d³ = 6m/(πρ), then take the cube root."
                ],
                "walkthrough": [
                  "The supplied expression m = πd³ρ/6 is the density relationship ρ = m/V written with the sphere volume V = πd³/6.",
                  "Rearranging for the diameter gives d³ = 6m/(πρ).",
                  "Substituting m = 7.5 kg and ρ = 8100 kg m⁻³: d³ = (6 × 7.5)/(π × 8100) = 45/25446.9 = 1.768×10⁻³ m³.",
                  "Taking the cube root: d = (1.768×10⁻³)^(1/3) = 0.121 m (or 0.12 m)."
                ],
