                "hints": [
                  "Use P = EI (or P = VI) to calculate the battery power output in each state from (b)(i).",
                  "Calculate P1 = 14 × 2.33 W and P2 = 14 × 1.0 W, then subtract to find the change in total power."
                ],
                "walkthrough": [
                  "The total electrical power produced by the battery is P = EI.",
                  "When R3 = 0 Ω, current I1 = 2.33 A, so power P1 = 14 × 2.333 = 32.67 W (or 32.2 W if 2.3 A is used).",
                  "When R3 = 24 Ω, current I2 = 1.0 A, so power P2 = 14 × 1.0 = 14.0 W.",
                  "Change in total power = P1 − P2 = 32.67 − 14.0 = 18.67 W ≈ 19 W (or 18 W using 2.3 A)."
                ],
